<title>USA: Ericsson says no slowdown in global market.</title>
<headline>Ericsson says no slowdown in global market.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Telefon AB L.M. Ericsson's sales activity remains strong across its markets, with no slowdown globally, despite slower-than-expected U.S. adoption of its next-generation cell phones, its chief executive said.</p>
<p>Lars Ramqvist, chief executive of the Swedish cellular equipment giant, made the comments in a press briefing ahead of a meeting with Wall Street analysts and institutional investors set to begin in New York at 1530 EDT/1930GMT.</p>
<p>&quot;Activity is still very strong,&quot; Ramqvist said in response to a question about the company's business trends for 1997. &quot;We have not seen any slowdown globally in market activity.&quot;</p>
</text>
